    <string name="limit_how_title">How do I raise it? (only once)</string>
    <string name="limit_step1">Turn on “Developer options”: Settings → About phone → Software information, then tap “Build number” 7 times.</string>
    <string name="limit_step2">In Developer options turn on “Wireless debugging” (Android 11 or newer) while connected to Wi-Fi.</string>
    <string name="limit_step3">Install Termux from F-Droid and type: pkg install android-tools</string>
    <string name="limit_step4">In Wireless debugging tap “Pair device with pairing code”, open Termux next to it (split screen) and type: adb pair localhost:PORT CODE, then adb connect localhost:PORT shown on the main page.</string>
    <string name="limit_step5">Copy this command and paste it into Termux:</string>
    <string name="limit_step6">Come back to this screen: a “Raise limit” button appears. You can turn wireless debugging off afterwards.</string>
    <string name="limit_alt">Or raise the limit directly, without giving Barq the permission:</string>
    <string name="limit_behaviour">Sending behaviour</string>
    <string name="respect_limit">Stay under Android\'s limit</string>
    <string name="respect_limit_sub">Sends as fast as the limit allows so sending never stops. Turn it off only if you will answer Android\'s question yourself.</string>
    <string name="auto_retry">Retry automatically</string>
    <string name="auto_retry_sub">A message that fails because of no signal or the limit is sent again by itself, up to 3 times.</string>
    <string name="limit_warning">Note: sending very fast to many people may make your carrier slow down or pause the SIM. Barq never sends anything you did not ask for.</string>
